    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-07",
      "edition": "Saturday 7 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad rift claim",
          "heading": "Jamie George says England squad are 'really upset' by Times rift report",
          "body": "The Times report says unhappy players wanted talks with head coach Steve Borthwick and Rugby Football Union chief executive Bill Sweeney in Argentina in July, citing concerns over man-management. Hooker Jamie George says the squad are unhappy with the article, insisting that \"a lot of it's untrue\" and that its timing, two days before Sunday's Test against Australia, was designed to divide them. Captain Maro Itoje called a leader's meeting to handle it. \"This is going to galvanise us,\" George said."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Italy lose Nacho Brex and Tommaso Menoncello to injury before Springboks",
