          "heading": "Archie Griffin sits out Wales captain's run but is not injured",
          "body": "Bath prop Archie Griffin skipped Friday's captain's run before Saturday's Nations Championship match against Japan at the Principality Stadium. WalesOnline understands he is not carrying an injury and the absence was a decision to manage his training load. He will start at tighthead in a front row featuring Nicky Smith and captain Dewi Lake. The 25-year-old has a reputation as an extremely mobile and dynamic prop."
