          "kicker": "Squad visit",
          "heading": "Angus Crichton drops into Wallabies training in England while rehabbing foot injury",
          "body": "Wallabies coach Les Kiss says new NSW Waratahs recruit Angus Crichton could be a real asset in the midfield, after the former Sydney Roosters star joined the group for training in England. Crichton, who is still rehabbing a stress fracture in his right foot, was over on holiday and lunched with the squad alongside Brisbane Lions player Will Ashcroft. Kiss said, \"I think initially the midfield, definitely. That's how I see it,\" and Crichton will head to Waratahs pre-season in the coming days."
        },
