          "kicker": "Japan history",
          "heading": "Ieuan Evans recalls 1993 try within 45 seconds against Japan in Cardiff",
          "body": "The try came off a wild pass from Japan's scrum-half, a loose ball Evans gathered on the 10-metre line before diving in at the right corner. It was the first full capped match between the sides, and Evans, Wales captain that day, later spoke Japanese at the post-match banquet using phonetic text written by Cardiff University's Business School. Wales won pretty convincingly, and Evans says Japanese rugby has since gone on to become a major force."
        },
